    <!--
            <question id="arch-overall" when="init">
                Describe the overall architecture.
                <hint>
                What will be API for
                <a href="https://netbeans.apache.org/wiki/API_Design#Separate_API_for_clients_from_support_API">
                    clients and what support API</a>?
                What parts will be pluggable?
                How will plug-ins be registered? Please use <code>&lt;api type="export"/&gt;</code>
                to describe your general APIs and specify their
                <a href="https://netbeans.apache.org/wiki/API_Stability#private">
                stability categories</a>.
                If possible please provide simple diagrams.
                </hint>
            </question>
    -->
    <answer id="arch-overall">
        <p>
            The module implements a project type for arbitrary directories. A directory
            becomes a generic project when it contains the marker file (a plain
            <code>java.util.Properties</code> file named <code>.nbgp</code> by default,
            brandable) or when the
            <code>org.netbeans.modules.generic.project</code> FileObject attribute is
            set on it (a marker-less "local" project). A generic project is just its
            directory: the logical view is a plain folder tree, and move, rename, copy
            and delete operate on the directory as a whole.
        </p>
        <p>
            The module exports no public Java packages; its contracts are:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <api group="java" name="GenericProjectType" type="export" category="devel">
                    <p>
                        The project type itself, discovered by <code>ProjectManager</code> via
                        the <code>ProjectFactory</code> registered in the global lookup. The
                        contract is the marker file/attribute detection and the auxiliary data
                        files (see <code>format-types</code>). The per-project services
                        (logical view, project information, operations, customizer) are
                        published in the project's lookup and can be extended by other modules
                        via <code>@ProjectServiceProvider</code>.
                    </p>
                </api>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </answer>



