                if the order is important, etc. Also classify the stability of such
                API contract. Use &lt;api group=&amp;lookup&amp; /&gt; tag, so
                your information gets listed in the summary page of your javadoc.
                </hint>
            </question>
    -->
    <answer id="lookup-lookup">
        <p>
            Yes. Each project's lookup is a composite rooted at
            <code>Projects/org-netbeans-modules-generic-project/Lookup</code>, so the
            module (and other modules) can provide per-project services that are found
            in the project's lookup.
        </p>
    </answer>



    <!--
            <question id="lookup-register" when="final">
